# Text files are stored with LF and checked out with LF on every platform, so a Windows
# checkout cannot change a file's bytes. Without this, core.autocrlf=true rewrote
# chinese-prompts.snapshot.txt to CRLF and the prompt-lock test failed on content that
# was identical (2026-10-23). macOS and Linux are unaffected: they already check out LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets keep their bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
